# Token efficiency (Cursor seat)

Complements `lean-output.mdc` (chat brevity). **Output length is the #1 conversation lever** — most per-turn cost is AI output; cut output X% → save ~X%. This rule covers **context** cost.

## Cursor settings (baked, not negotiated at runtime)

- **Auto mode default** for routine work; **Max Mode OFF** globally
- **Model fixed at job start** — no mid-session model switch (invalidates cache)
- Prefer `@`-references + `.cursorignore` over broad index / whole-repo context
- Cap project rules (`.cursor/rules/`, legacy `.cursorrules`) — trim domain rules to path-scoped files; keep global rules lean

## Subagent offload

See `right-model-routing.mdc` — default **solo**; witness WHO on Vellum before spawn; **never** `model: inherit` on subagents.

Delegate to Task/subagents when the main thread would load heavy context:

- Exploring unknown code (>2 files you have not read this session)
- Log/build/test output (>100 lines)
- External docs or URLs (summarise in subagent; parent gets summary only)

Subagent transcripts stay isolated — only the final summary returns to the parent.

## CLI over MCP (read-only doors)

MCP injects all tool schemas every turn (high token cost). For read-only lookups (Brain, Research, CRM, GitHub reads): **CLI/shell first**, MCP only where OAuth/audit/caching earn it. Code-execution / progressive disclosure for large APIs.

## File-read discipline

- **Glob/Grep first**, Read second — name paths before opening files
- Use Read `limit` / `offset` for large files; never paste full file contents back
- Prefer `head`, `rg`, targeted reads over unbounded `find`, `tree`, `cat` on lockfiles/minified assets

## Ignore discipline

Respect `.gitignore` and `.cursorignore` at project roots. Always exclude from reads/search when not already ignored:

`node_modules/`, `dist/`, `build/`, `.next/`, `coverage/`, `vendor/`, `*.min.js`, `*.map`, `.venv/`, `__pycache__/`, `.pytest_cache/`, `target/`

## LLM config

**No stop sequences** in fleet LLM calls — they truncate legitimate output. Use `MAX_TOKENS` only.

## Frontier tokens = judgment only

Opus/plans once; execution is mechanical. If a step is "tricky," fix the plan — do not escalate the executor or reload heavy context in the parent thread.

## Compaction

When context compacts, `preCompact` hook preserves task snapshots under `~/.cursor/compact-backups/`. After compact, re-state open task + file list in one structured block.

## Prompts

Prefer structured fields (`File:` / `Bug:` / `Action:`) over long narrative walls.

